# WinMix — project briefing and working rules for the AI assistant

Read this whole message before touching anything. It is the single source of truth about the current state. If any file in the repo contradicts it, THIS message wins and you must tell me about the conflict instead of silently picking a side.

## 1. What WinMix is

A personal analytics and prediction tool for virtual football (leagues: `angol`, `spanyol`; 16 teams, 240 matches per season). I am the ONLY user. There is no multi-user, multi-tenant, or public-facing requirement. Do not add features for other users.

Intended flow:
1. Full match history comes from a sealed, versioned cloud dataset (Supabase).
2. One shared model (shared bivariate score matrix -> 1X2, BTTS, Over/Under, team-goal markets) with walk-forward, prequential calibration (no look-ahead).
3. For each round I enter the fixtures; the app proposes "Top 3+3" candidates, gated by BTTS/underdog veto, evidence level and reliability bands, and builds slips.
4. I record results; the prediction ledger grades them and the calibration refits.
5. Every decision must be explainable (Pipeline Audit, decision trace).

Pages (`src/pages`): DataStudio, LeagueAnalyzer, HeadToHead, FixturePredictor, PredictionLedger, PipelineAudit, PipelineOperationsDashboard.

