## 3. Current state (verified 2026-10-22)

Database (public schema), tables with data: `winmix_matches` (~72.7k rows incl. all versions), `winmix_seasons`, `winmix_teams` (32), `winmix_markets` (23), `winmix_data_versions` (5), `winmix_ingest_receipts` (4), `winmix_cloud_operators` (1).
Current sealed version: 103 seasons = 62 `angol` + 41 `spanyol` = 24,720 matches.
There are NO tables for slips, ledger, fixtures, rounds or calibration history. Slips and ledger live only in the browser (localStorage). This is the biggest functional gap.

Data model: immutable versioned data (`winmix_data_versions`: draft/sealed/superseded, `is_current`, `revision`, `fingerprint`). Sealed rows are trigger-protected. Reads go through RPCs `winmix_cloud_access`, `winmix_cloud_versions`, `winmix_cloud_seasons`, `winmix_cloud_season`, `winmix_cloud_ratings`. Writes go only through the Edge Function `winmix-ingest` -> `winmix_ingest_v2` (service-only).

Hash caveat: the local `contentHash` is a `simpleHash`; the server `content_hash` is canonical sha256. They are NOT comparable. Compare cloud versions by `id + revision + fingerprint`, never by per-season hash.

Frontend branches (do not assume they are merged; check `git branch -a` and the remote first):
- `perf/idb-cache-and-parallel-downloads` — IndexedDB pipeline cache (`src/utils/pipelineCache.ts`, restored on boot in `useWinmixEngine.ts`), bounded parallel season download (`fetchCloudSeasonsConcurrently`, concurrency 8). Awaiting my browser verification, then merge.
- `feat/cloud-freshness-notice` (on top of the perf branch) — stores the downloaded cloud version marker (`src/utils/cloudFreshness.ts`) and shows a non-blocking toast when the cloud has a newer version. Notification only; never overwrites local data.
- `main` has moved since these branches were cut. Rebase-free approach: merge `main` INTO a feature branch (not rebase), then re-run all checks.

Known performance root cause that was fixed on the perf branch: 103 per-season RPC calls fired at once, CSV rebuild, and a full browser pipeline recompute on every load, with the IndexedDB cache unused.

